        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 必要",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "必要 — bìyào — \"necessary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我觉得没有必要问这个问题 wǒ juéde méiyǒu bìyào wèn zhège wèntí — I don't think there's any need to ask that."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 必 (bì) — five strokes: a dot on the left, the long curve along the foot that hooks up, as in 心, a dot on top, a long left-falling stroke down through the curve, and a dot on the right. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "必要 (bìyào) is built from bì and 要 'to need', both inherited from Middle Chinese, pjit and 'jiewH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'certain' and 'so', and the second 'to bind'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
